---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About — Bhupesh Parmar"
  description="Product designer with two design degrees, a year in the field, and a habit of explaining the reasoning behind every screen."
>
  <section class="page about">
    <div class="page__inner">
      <p class="about__kicker">About</p>
      <h1 class="work__title">Hi, I&rsquo;m Bhupesh.</h1>
      <div class="prose about__prose">
        <p>
          I&rsquo;m a product designer. I take products that are hard to use,
          or businesses that are stuck doing things by hand, and turn them into
          something people can pick up without a manual. I care most about the
          part before the screens: working out what is actually wrong, and
          being able to explain every decision afterwards in plain language.
        </p>

        <h2>Where I&rsquo;ve been</h2>
        <p>
          I have two design degrees, a B.Des from Chitkara University and an
          M.Des in Product Design from UPES, and about a year of professional
          work in between and around them. At <a href="/work/ikarus-configurator">Ikarus 3D</a>{' '}
          I worked on an internal platform for building 3D product
          configurators, and on <a href="/work/ikarus-nest">Nest</a>, a
          marketplace for 3D-printable files where 43 interviews changed what
          the product was for. Most recently I designed the{' '}
          <a href="/work/tbs">client app</a> and{' '}
          <a href="/work/tbs-dashboard">trainer dashboard</a> for TBS, a
          fitness coaching business that had outgrown WhatsApp.
        </p>
        <p>
          Across those, the same three things keep coming up: research that
          overturns the brief, information architecture (deciding what goes
          where, and what goes first), and design systems that let a small team
          ship a lot of screens consistently.
        </p>

        <h2>What I&rsquo;m looking for</h2>
        <p>
          A product team where I can own a problem end to end, from the
          conversations that define it to the handoff, and where being able to
          argue for a decision matters as much as drawing it. Consumer or
          enterprise, I&rsquo;ve done both and liked both.
        </p>

        <h2>How I work</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><b>Plain language first.</b> If I can&rsquo;t explain a decision to someone outside the team, it isn&rsquo;t finished.</li>
          <li><b>Show the trade-off.</b> Every decision on this site says what it cost, not just what it won.</li>
          <li><b>Prototype early.</b> A link people can click settles more in a day than a week of slide reviews.</li>
          <li><b>No invented numbers.</b> Where a project has no results yet, the case study says so.</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="about__cta">
          <a class="about__btn" href="mailto:designs.bhupesh@gmail.com">Say hello</a>
          <a class="about__btn about__btn--ghost" href="/Bhupesh-Parmar-Resume.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View my r&eacute;sum&eacute;</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .about__kicker {
    margin: 0 0 10px;
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 1.8px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--blue-500);
  }
  .about__prose { margin-top: 28px; }
  .about__prose h2 {
    font-size: 30px;
    margin-top: 1.6em;
  }
  .about__prose li b { color: #0b0d12; }
  .about__cta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; margin-top: 36px; }
  .about__btn {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 13px 22px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--blue-500);
    color: #fff !important;
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
    font-size: 14.5px;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: none !important;
    transition: transform 0.2s ease, background 0.2s ease;
  }
  .about__btn:hover { transform: translateY(-2px); background: var(--blue-700); }
  .about__btn--ghost {
    background: #fff;
    color: #0b0d12 !important;
    border: 1px solid #dfe3ea;
  }
  .about__btn--ghost:hover { background: #f4f6fa; }
</style>
